From 4e6ef275dbb61b53d2077515763da5bb46f3f6f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FIELD CI <claude@field.dev>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:31:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: no opening line is written once its game has started

snapshotCronOdds selects rows with finalized_at IS NULL, so a game in
progress gets through, and the live feed still lists it. 7 of the 191
odds_api opening writes since 10-01 were captured after kickoff (MLB 3,
CFL 2, MLS 1, WNBA 1, up to 241 minutes in; D1, 2026-10-23). The worker
backfill stamps its noon historical snapshot, so a game that tipped before
noon was in play.

Both writers now skip a line whose capture instant is at or after the
row's kickoff, or the vendor's commence for a row that has no kickoff.
kickoffMark reads an unreadable instant as unknown, never as late, so it
refuses nothing it cannot judge. Both SELECTs gain start_time; their WHERE
clauses and the backfill's deliberately unguarded finality are unchanged.
A refused backfill row is skipped like a miss, so a date holding only such
rows is still marked tried.

This is the first commit of shape (a) of
docs/CC-CMD-2026-10-21-historical-closing-join-misses-four-sports.md. It
stands alone with today's join, and the next commit gives the join its
per-team rule.

scripts/check-odds-join-shared.mjs runs the REAL snapshotCronOdds and
runOddsBackfillForDate, text-extracted with each anchor asserted unique,
over node:sqlite with a stubbed vendor. It checks:
- the refusal on each clock alone, for both writers and both backfill
  tables;
- the kickoff instant itself;
- that index.js imports every helper the harness hands the writers.
6 of 6 pass, and the 5 refusal scenarios fail against the parent.

mutate-odds-join-shared works on copies of the source and counts a mutant
only when its named scenario fails: 10 of 10. mutate-odds-writers-sport-
scoped's M1 anchor moves with the cron SELECT. The harness hardening came
from an adversarial review (workflow wf_ffee75ef-5a0).

