From 7aa907f96d097864670931e31e74f0b864e53c32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FIELD CI <claude@field.dev>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:31:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix: one per-team join behind the three odds writers that
 match by name

findOddsForRow matched a row to a vendor event by both teams' resolved
keys. For NBA, NHL, CFB and NFL that never matched: the archive stores
'Capitals', 'Knicks', 'Missouri St', the vendor 'Washington Capitals', and
no alias joins them. So the opening cron, the worker backfill and the
/archive/game closing write paid for those sports and wrote nothing. The
pair map also kept the LAST event listed for a pairing, so a series or a
doubleheader could price a row from another game.

Shape (a) of
docs/CC-CMD-2026-10-21-historical-closing-join-misses-four-sports.md,
as the owner ruled it:
- with a readable kickoff, a side matches on its resolved key or its name
  tokens (the rule AmbientDO's capture runs), and the vendor event must
  start within 90 minutes;
- exactly one listing may qualify, as listed;
- a row with no kickoff keeps the old rule (resolved keys, as listed),
  now also exactly once;
- the three callers hand the join the row's start_time.

The closing path now matches the four sports too, so the noon snapshot
becomes their closing line. The owner ruled that knowing it lands about
13 hours before kickoff, where the CI backfill's line lands 21-82 minutes
before.

Reversed listings are not accepted. Each row is decided alone, so a split
squad (same clubs, same instant, two cities; three NHL preseason pairs)
had one listing price both rows, one from the other game. Reversed
acceptance gained 1 row in 768 recorded pairs.

JOIN_UNWRITABLE gets an end date instead of being deleted, so the demand
script still keeps pre-fix days' unwritable fetches out of demand.

Harness (scripts/check-odds-join-shared.mjs, the real writers on
node:sqlite):
- on 165 recorded rows, the four sports go from 0 to 110 of 112 right,
  0 wrong; MLS from 40 to 41 of 43; MLB, CFL and WNBA unchanged;
- the 09-12 CFB full feed: 73 right, 0 wrong;
- covered: a split squad, doubleheader twins either side, several
  listings with and without a kickoff, a cup row with no kickoff, an NBA
  game in progress at the snapshot, the closing write.
19 of 19 pass; 21 of 21 mutations caught.

Gates:
- G4 gains kickoff-bearing cases, and its N5 anchor moves: 43 of 43, 7 of
  7 caught.
- G5 gains a kickoff case and S6: 27 of 27, 5 of 5.
- The demand script: 21 of 21.

A design pass, two critics and an adversarial review (workflows
wf_0d274771-67f and wf_ffee75ef-5a0) shaped this commit. Every finding
was verified.

